---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import TokenCounter from '../../components/TokenCounter.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI Token Counter"
  description="Estimate how many tokens your text will use across GPT, Claude, Gemini, and Llama — instantly, no signup."
>
  <TokenCounter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why token count matters</h2>
  <p>
    AI APIs charge and enforce limits by tokens, not characters or words —
    and a token isn't a fixed unit across models. Knowing your token count
    before you send a request helps you stay under context limits and
    predict cost accurately.
  </p>

  <h2>How this estimate works</h2>
  <p>
    This tool uses published average characters-per-token ratios for each
    model family to give a fast, client-side estimate. It won't be
    byte-for-byte identical to what the provider's API reports, but it's
    close enough for planning prompts and estimating cost.
  </p>

  <h2>AI Token Counter FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why isn't this 100% exact?</strong> Exact tokenization depends
    on each provider's specific tokenizer (e.g. OpenAI's tiktoken), which
    splits text into subword units based on a trained vocabulary — not a
    simple character ratio. This tool trades small accuracy for instant,
    dependency-free results.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does punctuation or code count differently?</strong> Yes — code
    and non-English text often tokenize less efficiently than plain English
    prose, so actual counts may run higher than this estimate for those
    cases.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
